  "description": "IJOKOK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C216 H184 Dy16 N34 O74 P10,C1 H4 O1,9(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5B (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.768-4.379 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.50-125.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C217H204Dy16N34O84P10.",
